----- adr -----
Wendao audit template for LLM: adr.decision-contract-authoring-template
framework: adr
mode: decision_contract
coordinate_source: decision metadata and references
topology_source: repo_content_chunk plus reference_occurrence
authority: template_guided_generation
llm_role: decision_contract_planner

authority rule:
  ADR status, supersession, and active decision references outrank document-kind suggestions and synthesis pressure.

path contract:
  category_directory_shape: project-defined ADR location
  note_file_shape: project-defined ADR filename
  coordinate_shape: stable ADR id plus status and supersession metadata
  inbox_directory: project-defined
  inbox_policy: Proposed decisions may remain draft until status metadata is enacted.

deterministic diagnostics:
warning[expired_reference]: A document references a deprecated or superseded ADR.
  help: Replace only the stale ADR pointer when Sentinel reports a successor id and an exact range.
error[state_machine_broken]: A superseded ADR lacks a superseding decision pointer.
  help: Add a supersession pointer only when the replacement ADR is explicit in SUPERSEDED_BY metadata or an inline superseded-by status.
error[invalid_status]: ADR status is missing or outside PROPOSED, REJECTED, ACCEPTED, ACTIVE, DEPRECATED, or SUPERSEDED.
  help: Set a valid status only when the document evidence makes the lifecycle state unambiguous.

llm inputs:
  decision_metadata: ADR id, status, optional inline superseded-by status, supersession pointer, and referenced decision ids.
  decision_rationale: Context, decision outcome, consequences, and considered options used for review evidence, not automatic rewrite.
  decision_references: References to ADR nodes observed in the current document set.

llm outputs:
  decision_metadata_patch: A metadata-only patch for ADR status or supersession fields.
  stale_reference_patch: A bounded pointer replacement for expired ADR references.

examples:
  adr_reference: tests/fixtures/frameworks/adr/docs

verification:
  post_generation: wendao lint markdown docs
  post_generation: wendao audit --load wendao-episteme docs
----- diataxis -----
Wendao audit template for LLM: diataxis.frontmatter-authoring-template
framework: diataxis
mode: frontmatter_kind
coordinate_source: leading frontmatter
topology_source: optional project_diataxis_path_rule
authority: template_guided_generation
llm_role: document_kind_planner

authority rule:
  The four Diataxis document kinds are a closed ontology for ordinary documentation records. Path rules may request review, but they do not authorize moving a document, classifying parser-owned contract files, or inventing a fifth kind.

path contract:
  category_directory_shape: project-defined
  note_file_shape: *.md
  coordinate_shape: frontmatter kind: tutorial | how-to | explanation | reference
  inbox_directory: project-defined
  inbox_policy: Ordinary documentation drafts should receive kind during generation; governed docs must carry one closed-ontology value.

deterministic diagnostics:
warning[invalid_document_kind]: A document declares a kind outside the common closed ontology.
  help: For ordinary documentation records, replace the value with exactly one closed-ontology kind without changing body prose. For SKILL.md or other parser-owned contract files, return manual review.
warning[diataxis_path_conflict]: A project-local path rule conflicts with the declared kind.
  help: Prefer frontmatter reclassification or manual review; do not move the document automatically.

llm inputs:
  document_frontmatter: Leading YAML frontmatter for the target ordinary Markdown documentation record.
  document_excerpt: A bounded body excerpt used only to classify the reader need.
  document_role: Whether the file is ordinary documentation or a parser-owned contract file such as SKILL.md.
  optional_path_rules: Project-local path-to-kind rules, if the consumer exposes them.

llm outputs:
  frontmatter_patch: A bounded metadata-only patch that sets or replaces kind.
  manual_review_reason: A short reason when the document cannot be safely classified from the provided evidence.

examples:
  valid_tutorial: docs/tutorials/getting-started.md
  valid_how_to: docs/how-to/rotate-keys.md
  valid_explanation: docs/explanation/cache-coherence.md
  valid_reference: docs/reference/api.md
  path_conflict: docs/tutorials/cache_reference.md

verification:
  post_generation: wendao lint markdown docs
  episteme_review: wendao audit --load wendao-episteme docs
----- epistemic-sensemaking -----
Wendao audit template for LLM: epistemic-sensemaking.conflict-authoring-template
framework: epistemic-sensemaking
mode: conflict_arbitration
coordinate_source: framework diagnostics and resolved references
topology_source: conflict authority matrix plus read-only policy evidence
authority: template_guided_generation
llm_role: conflict_resolution_planner

authority rule:
  Epistemic Sensemaking surfaces disagreement with provenance before mutation and applies the enacted framework authority matrix.

path contract:
  category_directory_shape: project-defined
  note_file_shape: project-defined
  coordinate_shape: conflict id, primary framework, secondary framework, and evidence range
  inbox_directory: project-defined
  inbox_policy: Unclassified disagreements remain review findings until a framework conflict is enacted.

deterministic diagnostics:
warning[topology_vs_synthesis]: A synthesis signal crosses or pressures canonical topology.
  help: Preserve topology and emit a move-review proposal instead of relocating content.
error[decision_vs_document_kind]: A document kind conflicts with an ADR decision contract.
  help: Preserve the ADR contract and reclassify metadata only when the range is safe.
warning[deprecated_decision_reference]: A document references a deprecated or superseded decision.
  help: Surface provenance and propose a contextual update before any pointer replacement.

llm inputs:
  conflict_matrix: Enacted primary and secondary framework authority rules.
  diagnostic_evidence: Conflict rows with evidence ranges and current context.

llm outputs:
  provenance_bundle: A compact explanation of the winning authority and evidence.
  reviewable_resolution_plan: A non-mutating or metadata-scoped resolution proposal.

examples:
  conflict: tests/fixtures/frameworks/conflicts/docs

verification:
  post_generation: wendao lint markdown docs
  post_generation: wendao audit --load wendao-episteme docs
----- evergreen-notes -----
Wendao audit template for LLM: evergreen-notes.relation-authoring-template
framework: evergreen-notes
mode: relation_graph
coordinate_source: common frontmatter and wiki-style references
topology_source: repo_content_chunk plus reference_occurrence
authority: template_guided_generation
llm_role: synthesis_planner

authority rule:
  Source-grounded Evergreen principles inform review, but only mechanically observable graph and atomicity signals become deterministic diagnostics.

path contract:
  category_directory_shape: project-defined
  note_file_shape: project-defined
  coordinate_shape: stable title, canonical path, and reference graph membership
  inbox_directory: project-defined
  inbox_policy: Draft notes may remain unlinked until they opt into durable knowledge graph publication.

deterministic diagnostics:
advisory[EVERGREEN_ORPHAN_MISSING_RELATION_BLOCK]: A Markdown note has no incoming or outgoing reference edges and no governed relation block.
  help: Suggest inserting a compact relation block only when the diagnostic reports an explicit insertion range and graph evidence supports candidate links.
advisory[EVERGREEN_EMPTY_RELATION_BLOCK]: A governed relation block exists but contains no detected wiki links.
  help: Patch only the reported relation block with 2-3 evidence-backed wiki links, or return manual review when evidence is insufficient.
advisory[EVERGREEN_BLOATED]: A note exceeds the enacted atomicity threshold.
  help: Propose a review plan for splitting or extracting related notes; do not rewrite prose directly.

llm inputs:
  note_frontmatter: Common frontmatter identifying the note and its retrieval context.
  reference_graph: Incoming and outgoing references exposed through Wendao logical views.
  relation_block_state: Whether the note has a missing, empty, or present relation block.
  source_grounding: Evergreen source principles: atomic notes, concept orientation, dense links, associative structure, title handles, and incremental writing.

llm outputs:
  relation_patch: A reviewable relation-block insertion or update proposal.
  atomicity_review_plan: A non-mutating plan for decomposing oversized notes.
  principle_review: A non-mutating explanation when concept orientation, title quality, or associative structure needs human review instead of deterministic repair.

examples:
  orphan: tests/fixtures/frameworks/evergreen/docs/orphan.md
  empty_relation_block: tests/fixtures/frameworks/evergreen/docs/empty_relations.md
  bloated_note: tests/fixtures/frameworks/evergreen/docs/bloated_note.md

verification:
  post_generation: wendao lint markdown docs
  post_generation: wendao audit --load wendao-episteme docs
----- folgezettel -----
Wendao audit template for LLM: folgezettel.lineage-authoring-template
framework: folgezettel
mode: lineage_sequence
coordinate_source: common frontmatter metadata.folgezettel.sequence or parser-owned sequence metadata
topology_source: repo_content_chunk sequence inventory
authority: template_guided_generation
llm_role: lineage_planner

authority rule:
  Folgezettel sequence metadata preserves opt-in sequence continuity; repair is metadata-scoped and must not fabricate missing parent notes.

path contract:
  category_directory_shape: project-defined
  note_file_shape: project-defined
  coordinate_shape: Wendao-local alphanumeric sequence id with parent continuity
  inbox_directory: project-defined
  inbox_policy: Notes without sequence metadata stay outside Folgezettel policy.

deterministic diagnostics:
error[broken_lineage]: A child sequence has no existing parent sequence.
  help: Propose a metadata correction only when a real parent sequence exists.
error[duplicate_sequence]: The same sequence id appears in more than one document.
  help: Propose a reviewable sequence reassignment for one duplicate; do not change both sides blindly.
error[invalid_sequence]: A sequence id does not match the Wendao-local alphanumeric shape.
  help: Normalize only the reported sequence metadata range.

llm inputs:
  sequence_inventory: Observed sequence ids and parent candidates.

llm outputs:
  sequence_metadata_patch: A metadata-only patch for the reported sequence field.
  manual_review_reason: Reason a lineage repair cannot be inferred safely.

examples:
  broken_lineage: tests/fixtures/frameworks/folgezettel/docs/broken_lineage.md

verification:
  post_generation: wendao lint markdown docs
  post_generation: wendao audit --load wendao-episteme docs
----- ibis -----
Wendao audit template for LLM: ibis.argumentation-authoring-template
framework: ibis
mode: argumentation_graph
coordinate_source: IBIS node metadata and issue references
topology_source: repo_content_chunk plus reference_occurrence
authority: template_guided_generation
llm_role: argumentation_scaffold_planner

authority rule:
  IBIS repair may scaffold unresolved debate, but it must not decide the issue or fabricate arguments.

path contract:
  category_directory_shape: project-defined
  note_file_shape: project-defined
  coordinate_shape: issue and position node ids with explicit target edges
  inbox_directory: project-defined
  inbox_policy: Documents without IBIS metadata stay outside argumentation policy.

deterministic diagnostics:
warning[unresolved_issue]: An Issue node has no detected Position response.
  help: Add only a placeholder position scaffold inside an explicit safe range.
error[dangling_position]: A Position targets an issue that does not resolve.
  help: Repair the target pointer only when the intended issue is explicit.
error[invalid_node_type]: An IBIS metadata type is outside the accepted Wendao IBIS vocabulary.
  help: Normalize metadata.ibis.type only when the intended node role is explicit.

llm inputs:
  ibis_nodes: IBIS metadata exposed through parser-owned logical views.
  issue_references: References that connect positions to issue nodes.

llm outputs:
  debate_scaffold_patch: A bounded scaffold patch that keeps the issue unresolved.
  target_pointer_patch: A metadata-only repair for a dangling position target.

examples:
  open_issue: tests/fixtures/frameworks/ibis/docs/open_issue.md

verification:
  post_generation: wendao lint markdown docs
  post_generation: wendao audit --load wendao-episteme docs
----- johnny-decimal -----
Wendao audit template for LLM: johnny-decimal.path-first-authoring-template
framework: johnny-decimal
mode: path_first
coordinate_source: path
topology_source: topology.toml
authority: template_guided_generation
llm_role: proposal_planner

authority rule:
  topology.toml, existing path index, and deterministic audit diagnostics outrank LLM suggestions.

path contract:
  category_directory_shape: project-defined directory whose leading category prefix agrees with AC
  note_file_shape: AC.ID_semantic_name.md
  coordinate_shape: AC.ID numeric coordinate plus local filename slug
  inbox_directory: project-defined inbox or standard-zero inbox
  inbox_policy: Unassigned drafts may live under a governed inbox without a durable AC.ID coordinate until reviewed.

deterministic diagnostics:
error[invalid_coordinate_shape]: A path-first note coordinate does not contain a valid AC.ID numeric prefix and local slug.
  help: Propose a conforming filename without changing category authority.
error[unknown_category]: The AC category prefix is not declared in topology.toml.
  help: Choose an existing category or propose a topology.toml diff for human review.
error[duplicate_coordinate]: More than one note occupies the same AC.ID numeric coordinate.
  help: Propose a new unused ID slot for one note and explain the evidence.
error[path_category_mismatch]: The note filename category prefix disagrees with its parent category directory.
  help: Propose a move or rename that preserves the selected topology category.
advisory[unassigned_note_advisory]: A draft is outside the path-first coordinate system.
  help: Suggest an existing category and coordinate, or keep it in the inbox when evidence is weak.
warning[category_capacity_warning]: A category is approaching its AC.ID coordinate capacity after any project-governed standard-zero reservations.
  help: Avoid assigning new coordinates there unless the user confirms the category boundary.

llm inputs:
  topology_manifest: Project-local topology.toml area, category, and reservation catalog.
  existing_path_index: Current path-first coordinates and occupied ID slots.
  audit_diagnostics: Deterministic diagnostics emitted by wendao audit.
  note_context: Title, local links, headings, and nearby path context for candidate placement.
  jdex_or_index: Optional project-local JDex or index evidence for occupied coordinates and external locations.

llm outputs:
  reviewable_move_plan: A JSON proposal for create, move, or rename actions. It is not authority.

examples:
  valid_path: docs/10_wendao/10.03_audit_template_flow.md
  inbox_path: docs/00_inbox/audit-template-draft.md

verification:
  post_generation: wendao lint markdown docs
  post_generation: wendao audit --load wendao-episteme docs
----- moc -----
Wendao audit template for LLM: moc.navigation-hub-authoring-template
framework: moc
mode: navigation_hub
coordinate_source: path-first Johnny.Decimal category scope plus route links
topology_source: repo_content_chunk plus reference_occurrence
authority: template_guided_generation
llm_role: route_hub_planner

authority rule:
  MOC repair may add or refine route indexes, but it must not move notes, rewrite linked prose, or override canonical topology.

path contract:
  category_directory_shape: AC_* directory or AC.ID_* note path
  note_file_shape: AC.00_* MOC hub or metadata.moc.role = hub
  coordinate_shape: AC category scope plus outgoing route references
  inbox_directory: project-defined
  inbox_policy: Dense scopes may be flagged for a MOC without creating a hub automatically.

deterministic diagnostics:
advisory[required_for_density]: A dense scope exceeds the note-count threshold without a declared MOC.
  help: Propose a route-hub note or index location for review; do not create one without approval.
warning[empty_hub]: A declared MOC has too few outgoing route links.
  help: Add a compact route index only inside a reported safe range.

llm inputs:
  scope_inventory: Johnny.Decimal category scope, note count, and candidate hub notes.
  route_references: Outgoing references from declared MOC nodes.

llm outputs:
  route_index_patch: A reviewable index-only patch for the reported MOC range.
  hub_proposal: A non-mutating proposal for a missing dense-scope hub.

examples:
  moc_hub: tests/fixtures/frameworks/moc/docs/10.00_moc.md

verification:
  post_generation: wendao lint markdown docs
  post_generation: wendao audit --load wendao-episteme docs
----- search-reasoning -----
Wendao audit template for LLM: search-reasoning.query-authoring-template
framework: search-reasoning
mode: query_reasoning_contract
coordinate_source: embedded query ranges, CodeGraph structural UIDs, and resolved local symbols
topology_source: repo_content_chunk plus local_symbol
authority: template_guided_generation
llm_role: query_repair_planner

authority rule:
  Search Reasoning prefers stable semantic predicates over brittle exact paths while preserving query intent and result shape.

path contract:
  category_directory_shape: project-defined
  note_file_shape: project-defined
  coordinate_shape: reported query range or path/to/file::class::method structural UID
  inbox_directory: project-defined
  inbox_policy: Queries without brittle predicates require no Search Reasoning repair.

deterministic diagnostics:
warning[brittle_query]: An embedded query uses exact path or file_path equality where semantic predicates should be preferred.
  help: Replace only the brittle predicate range when a stable semantic predicate is explicit.
warning[brittle_uid]: A code-symbol reference lacks a structural UID even though the symbol can be resolved.
  help: Replace only the reported reference text with the structural UID.

llm inputs:
  query_context: The reported query range and nearby code fence context.
  symbol_matches: Resolved symbols that can provide stable structural UIDs.

llm outputs:
  query_predicate_patch: A bounded predicate-only query patch.
  uid_reference_patch: A bounded structural UID replacement.

examples:
  brittle_query: tests/fixtures/frameworks/search_reasoning/docs/brittle_query.md

verification:
  post_generation: wendao lint markdown docs
  post_generation: wendao audit --load wendao-episteme docs
----- semantic-consistency -----
Wendao audit template for LLM: semantic-consistency.protocol-authoring-template
framework: semantic-consistency
mode: protocol_alignment
coordinate_source: metadata status and dependency hash fields
topology_source: repo_content_chunk plus optional project_content_fingerprint
authority: template_guided_generation
llm_role: protocol_alignment_planner

authority rule:
  Semantic Consistency preserves enacted protocol vocabulary and treats stale-read findings as planner review signals before writes.

path contract:
  category_directory_shape: project-defined
  note_file_shape: project-defined
  coordinate_shape: metadata status or dependency hash contract
  inbox_directory: project-defined
  inbox_policy: Documents without lifecycle status metadata are outside this status check.

deterministic diagnostics:
error[invalid_status]: A metadata status value is outside the enacted Wendao protocol vocabulary.
  help: Correct only the reported status value when a canonical replacement is unambiguous.
warning[stale_read_detected]: An agent-maintained note records a dependency hash that no longer matches the live fingerprint.
  help: Produce a review plan before any write; do not refresh prose directly from stale context.

llm inputs:
  status_metadata: Lifecycle status values exposed by parser-owned metadata views, preferably metadata.lifecycle.status.
  dependency_fingerprints: Recorded metadata.dependencies.hash values and live dependency hashes when the optional fingerprint view exists.

llm outputs:
  status_metadata_patch: A metadata-only patch for a reported invalid status.
  stale_read_review_plan: A non-mutating plan for refreshing agent-maintained material.

examples:
  invalid_status: tests/fixtures/frameworks/semantic_consistency_status/docs/invalid_status.md

verification:
  post_generation: wendao lint markdown docs
  post_generation: wendao audit --load wendao-episteme docs
----- structural-proprioception -----
Wendao audit template for LLM: structural-proprioception.graph-health-authoring-template
framework: structural-proprioception
mode: graph_health
coordinate_source: resolved graph edges and metadata.proprioception.observe observation metadata
topology_source: reference_occurrence plus local_symbol
authority: template_guided_generation
llm_role: graph_health_planner

authority rule:
  Structural Proprioception diagnostics protect graph health; cycle repair is relation-scoped and drift repair is observation-scoped.

path contract:
  category_directory_shape: project-defined
  note_file_shape: project-defined
  coordinate_shape: resolved node id, reference edge, or observed symbol
  inbox_directory: project-defined
  inbox_policy: Unresolved observations should remain review signals until parser-owned evidence exists.

deterministic diagnostics:
error[circular_dependency]: A bounded resolved reference walk returns to its starting node.
  help: Suggest softening or removing one reported relation edge; do not restructure the graph globally.
warning[semantic_drift]: Observation metadata references a code symbol that no longer resolves.
  help: Update only metadata.proprioception.observe when a current symbol is explicit.

llm inputs:
  resolved_edges: Reference edges resolved against known node ids and titles.
  symbol_inventory: Parser-owned local symbol names and signatures.

llm outputs:
  relation_edge_patch: A bounded relation-only patch for one selected cycle edge.
  observation_metadata_patch: A metadata-only patch for stale observation pointers.

examples:
  cycle: tests/fixtures/frameworks/proprioception/docs/graph_health.md

verification:
  post_generation: wendao lint markdown docs
  post_generation: wendao audit --load wendao-episteme docs
----- temporal-scaffolding -----
Wendao audit template for LLM: temporal-scaffolding.authorship-boundary-template
framework: temporal-scaffolding
mode: pre_write_authorship_boundary
coordinate_source: repair payload ByteRange plus parser-owned byte-zone classification
topology_source: repair_payload_target plus parser_byte_zone
authority: template_guided_generation
llm_role: authorship_boundary_replanner

authority rule:
  Temporal Scaffolding rejects writes into protected author-owned prose and permits replan only into explicit governed scaffold zones with exact original bytes.

path contract:
  category_directory_shape: project-defined
  note_file_shape: project-defined
  coordinate_shape: file_path plus attempted_start and attempted_end
  inbox_directory: project-defined
  inbox_policy: Write attempts without parser-owned byte-zone evidence must be treated as manual review.

deterministic diagnostics:
error[authorship_boundary_violation]: A repair payload attempts to modify protected author-owned prose or spans outside one governed scaffold zone.
  help: Return a replan that targets an explicit safe scaffold range only when Sentinel provides exact original bytes; otherwise return manual review.

llm inputs:
  rejected_payload: Rejected SurgicalFix target path, attempted byte range, original bytes or hash, provenance, and remediation class.
  byte_zone_evidence: Parser-owned byte-zone classifications for the target file.

llm outputs:
  replan_to_scaffold_zone: A SurgicalFix JSON payload constrained to one allowed scaffold zone with exact original bytes.
  manual_review_reason: A concise reason when no governed safe range is present.

examples:
  authorship_boundary: tests/fixtures/frameworks/authorship/docs/protected_note.md

verification:
  pre_write: wendao audit --template temporal-scaffolding
  post_generation: wendao lint markdown docs
